The constructor-level pinning check is exact, and a ground witness gives the intended result. However, the static review has exposed a serious containment issue: several reusable rewrite rules match broader machine states than the claims that supposedly justify them. I’m now running bridge-free versus bridge-enabled ground configurations to determine whether this is merely an evidence gap or enables concretely false conclusions, as the Kit validation contract requires.
